Z||000003||fiero56||11-23-1999||10:25 PM||||I've tried getting one by dialing that number 6 times. The second I mention "Fiero" they refer me to FOCOA. One time I told them it was for a '88 Bonneville, but they got me when I gave them the VIN for the Fiero. "Thats a Fiero VIN, call this number blah, blah, blah..." I'll keep trying 'till I get one.||||reg||8
Z||000004||dogtired||11-24-1999||10:43 AM||||Got one about 6months ago, Pontiac was nice then. 1-800 Pontiac did care!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now it's 1-800 PONTIAC DON'T CARE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Tried again to get another for my other Fiero and for a while I thought I was talking to 1-800-FORD.<BR>We no longer do that!<BR>We no longer have cars that old in our computers!<BR>For recall info call FOCA?<BR>Fiero? didn't Dodge build that? (not really)<BR>All I got was a bunch of crappppppp!<BR>As a Fiero lover, I feel we are on our own, we all drive Fiero's a car that Pontiac built but will no longer support.||||reg||8
